+## NumPy admission successor
+
+The original f239ec1e handoff, its 33+63 files, pair and portable archive remain
+immutable. Independent root trusted-SDK review found a logical-buffer budget gap:
+a broadcast float32 scalar with shape (9437184,) became a TensorRef/raw ndarray
+with nbytes=37748736 but was charged zero by the Torch-only guard. The original
+microprobe remains many-oct7-handy-numpy-bound-review.log; it is trusted local
+admission evidence, not a guest/profile assertion. This successor corrects only
+pack-local value-work admission, adds focused tests, and refreshes this report and
+data/patch artifacts. IDs, schema, permissions, algorithms and stubs are unchanged.
+The browser fixture also now waits for the exact expected preview URL before its
+unchanged assertion: a retained second-run null-src failure showed that a widget
+commit is not the same observable event as a queued renderer update. No pack/UI
+algorithm or shared renderer is changed to make that readiness control pass.
+
+Plain numeric NumPy arrays now share the rank<=4/32MiB aggregate buffer budget.
+Logical nbytes is charged even for zero-copy broadcast/noncontiguous views. Closed
+dtype kinds bool/signed/unsigned/float/complex, itemsize1..32, preserve exact
+buffer dtype and native formatting with no coercion. Object, structured, string,
+unsupported and ndarray-subclass values are refused before formatting. Native
+Torch/array nonfinite buffer formatting remains admitted under the existing
+buffer profile; this does not relax the separate finite scalar policy.
+
+NumPy numeric scalar leaves and keys are charged their byte width and must be
+finite with magnitude<=1e6. Integer validation uses a Python integer solely for
+the bound comparison, avoiding fixed-width abs(minimum) overflow; the original
+scalar value/type is never replaced. Floating ceiling comparison does not narrow
+longdouble or cast the ceiling to float16 infinity. Non-numeric NumPy scalars are
+explicitly outside this numeric profile. Existing cumulative text/item/key/depth
+limits remain enforced, including mixed arrays/Torch/scalars/containers.
+
+Focused sentinels prove oversized broadcast buffers, mixed aggregate buffers,
+rank/dtype violations and scalar nonfinite/overflow/text/item cases fail before
+the native formatter runs. Fourteen dtype source controls cover 0D, contiguous,
+sliced and empty arrays plus numeric scalars with exact captured print text.
+Two fresh required guests execute manifest-registered PrintValue through the
+production outer boundary for admitted small arrays/scalars/mixed trees, proving
+owning array identity, dtype preservation, raw denial and recovery. No new host
+object recovery, shared API, dependency/profile quota or Cloud authority is added.
+
+## Bounds, runtime and persistence
+
+Local supported workload: aggregate tensor buffers <=32MiB, dense rank <=4;
+aggregate UTF8 text <=64KiB, cumulative container items <=4096 and depth <=8;
+finite scalar magnitude <=1e6. Whole projected output/copy and resampling kernel
+bytes are checked before algorithm allocation. Smart chunk durations 1..600s,
+variation below chunk length, finite FPS 1..240, cumulative silence RMS charge
+<=268435456 sample work, admitted flattened chunk-analysis duration <=60s.
+Speaker carrier <=4096 finite segments; logical labels <=1024 UTF8 bytes.
+Image encoded inputs <=16MiB with decoded float32/copy preflight; upload <=16MiB.
+PCM WAV admission <=4MiB/10s, sample widths 1..4, mono/stereo and rates
+8k/16k/44.1k/48k. PyDub's 24bit-to-32bit expansion is backend-specific evidence,
+not claimed Torchaudio 24bit identity. Dot-grid rendering is independently bounded.
+These are explicit local workload bounds, not source maxima or a host profile grant.
+
+Runtime declares Python >=3.13,<3.14 without dependency_profile_sha256. Active
+metadata pins pydub==0.25.1 and audioop-lts==0.2.2 on Python>=3.13; unused old
+Sherpa/FFmpeg requirements are removed from active metadata. The tested interpreter
+is root's isolated many-oct7-pydub-stage/venv/bin/python, with two offline verified
+wheels and inherited libraries. Observed Torch2.13.0/Torchaudio2.11.0/NumPy2.4.6/
+Pillow12.3.0/OpenCV5.0.0.93 identities are recorded, including duplicate AV dylib
+warnings. This is an unsealed Mac development/source-selection fixture, not a
+complete managed image or Linux native/dependency deployment attestation.
+
+Persistence disposition: workflow-serialized widgets and complete speaker carrier;
+managed input assets/labels and uploads belong to the host input catalogue. Fresh
+worker and workflow reconstruction are tested locally. No authored pack-local
+durable state is substituted with immutable defaults. Authenticated cloud asset
+ownership/import/backing-store continuity, multiserver identity and deployment
+remain unproved; no KV/global/browser cache is used to fake continuity.
+No trained model, accelerator, gpu-only/device-placement, general host allocation
+profile, universal media codec or broad arbitrary file compatibility is claimed.
